message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below. 若使用本作，请按下述格式引用。"
type: book
title: "选择的代价：完备、可组合与可传递的三维权衡——复杂知识系统如何形成、演化与更新 / The Price of Choice: The Impossibility Triangle of Completeness, Composability, and Transfer"
abstract: >-
  本著作提出“选择的代价”诊断框架，用以解释任何有限复杂度知识系统在形成、演化与更新中的结构性困境。 核心主张：完备（C）、可组合（A）、跨尺度传递（T）至多同时充分具备两项；选择两项，第三项必然留下可定位的缺口。信息子模性、离散—连续断层（1/3 缺口）与时间错配 τ 是三条理论见证。 结构与证据：25 章、附录 A—Y、38 幅图；医疗、教育、组织、金融（LTCM 1998）、软件工程、人工智能六个领域被放进同一张价目表，并配十个反例与逐条反驳条件。 诚实的纪律：全部主张按 A/B/C 与甲/乙/丙双重分级；37 个开放问题（O1—O37）标明已证、假设与待验证；失败与曾被推翻的强主张写在正文与附录，而非藏在脚注。 边界：框架给出“失效的形态与方向”的诊断，不给出新配置的预测，也不替代领域判断；它的用途是让设计者在选择两项时，看见第三项会怎样失效。 版本：2026-10-18，268 页，25 章，38 图，附录 A—Y，O1—O37；源码与脚本开源，内容 CC BY 4.0，代码 MIT。
  Abstract (English). This work presents “The Price of Choice,” a diagnostic framework for the structural dilemma of any finite-complexity knowledge system. Core thesis: completeness (C), composability (A) and cross-scale transfer (T) can be fully held at most two at a time; choosing two leaves an identifiable gap at the third. Information submodularity, the discrete–continuous gap (1/3) and temporal mismatch τ serve as theoretical witnesses. Structure and evidence: 25 chapters, appendices A–Y, 38 figures; six domains — medicine, education, organisations, finance (LTCM 1998), software engineering and AI — are mapped onto one price list, with ten counterexamples and refutation conditions. Discipline: every claim carries an evidence grade (A/B/C) and a conceptual grade; 37 open questions (O1–O37) mark what is proved, assumed or untested, and failures are reported in the main text. Boundaries: the framework diagnoses failure modalities and directions, not novel configurations, and does not replace domain expertise. Edition: 2026-10-18, 268 pages, 25 chapters, 38 figures, appendices A–Y.
